Description: Bayesian estimation of the additive main effects and
    multiplicative interaction (AMMI) model of multi-environment trials by
    the Gibbs sampler of Crossa, Perez-Elizalde, Jarquin, Cotes, Viele, Liu
    and Cornelius (2011) <doi:10.2135/cropsci2010.06.0343>: posterior
    distributions of the overall mean, genotype and environment effects,
    singular values, genotype and environment scores (von Mises-Fisher
    conditionals on the constrained spheres) and error variance; several
    chains with burn-in and thinning; posterior summaries with highest
    posterior density intervals; the convergence diagnostics of
    Raftery-Lewis, Heidelberger-Welch and Gelman-Rubin; the AMMI biplot with
    highest posterior density regions for inference on genotypes and
    environments; least-squares AMMI; and a plain-language interpretation of
    every result, computed from its numbers. Beyond the article: unbalanced
    trials with missing plots and cells (data augmentation),
    environment-specific error variances, the Bayesian GGE (sites
    regression) model of Perez-Elizalde, Jarquin and Crossa (2012)
    <doi:10.1007/s13253-011-0063-9>, probabilities of superior performance
    and stability (Dias et al. 2022 <doi:10.1007/s00122-022-04041-y>),
    posterior ranks, Bayesian stability measures, predictions and the
    winner of every environment, model choice by DIC and WAIC with
    posterior predictive checks, draws for the 'posterior', 'bayesplot'
    and 'coda' packages, a compiled sampler, and a built-in 'shiny'
    application. Bayesian stability analysis: the Finlay-Wilkinson,
    Eberhart-Russell and Shukla models by Gibbs sampling, and the posterior
    distributions of classical stability indices (Wricke, Shukla, Lin-Binns,
    Annicchiarico, Eskridge's safety-first) and of AMMI-based indices (ASV,
    SIPC, EV, Za, WAAS, WAASY). Every result prints the references of its
    method.
